WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:02.810
Really?

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.690
You were playing WIXOSS until four in the morning?

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.940
I showed it to Grandma, and she got hooked on it...

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.860
The loser had to peel the tangerines. See this?

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:13.570
All yellow!

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.280
Whoa, just how many times did you lose?

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.660
Oh, I forgot. You don't need to battle me anymore?

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:28.290
Yeah. Let's both become Eternal Girls,
and have each of our wishes come true!

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.470
But I don't really have any wishes or dreams...

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.550
C'mon, let's run!

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.140
Let's go.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.010
W-Wait up!

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.450
shinjitsu wa hitoe ni kaado no uraomote
Truth and reality are like the two sides of a card

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:03.960
tokenai mama
Forever entwined

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.750
mekurimekuru meku
Thrust upon this chaotic stage

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.710
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:13.970
memagurushii suteeji de
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:22.020
sono karamatta kanjou wo manzoku iku made nankai mo
Until I can finally sort out these mixed-up emotions

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.270
kowashite shimae
I'll destroy it countless times

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:30.360
unmei ni temaneki sare samayou ashita wa
The uncertain future will be summoned by fate

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:35.650
nani wo erande nani wo tebanashi hitotsu ni nareba iin darou
Should I choose just one thing to let go of?

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:41.410
najitta tefuda wo sarasu yoyuu nante nai yo
I can't afford to let my sinful hand show yet

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:46.500
kawaita koukai no umi wo nomihosu hibi wa
My days of leisurely drinking from the sea of regret are long over

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.840
kagirareta kotoba de itsushika no egao yurushite hoshiin darou
Will you really use your one wish to return that lost smile?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.050
utsutsu wo wasuretatte kamawanai yo dakara
It's no concern of mine if you avert your eyes from reality

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:02.810
ima wa shiranai de itai nee
So please just live in blissful ignorance

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.230
You know, finding Selectors is a real pain.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.780
There aren't many of them?

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:21.030
Yeah. You're the only other one in our school.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.620
Right, Hanayo-san?

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.660
Yes. I can recognize a Selector with one look.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.500
LRIGs are attracted to each other.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.380
For example, that girl over there...

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.630
Urazoe Iona?

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.390
She's really popular at the moment.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.850
She had a role in a drama recently,
and she's about to release a new single.

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.600
The girl next to her is one, too.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:45.850
Entire Issue - Cute & Cool

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:46.020
Let's all get lucky by
wearing lots of new
stylish clothes!
Entire Issue - Cute & Cool

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.190
I remember seeing her in
magazines every now and then.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:52.270
And her name was... um...

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.230
Akira!

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.020
Yeah, that's her! Huh?

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.320
Like, seriously? The 'zine model
Akira attends Go Middle School?

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.030
Wait—What was that just now?
Can you repeat that, please?!

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.120
H-Huh?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.750
Y-Yuzuki-san...

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.670
We've gotta strike when the iron is hot!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.920
I'll call dibs on her first and set up a match after school, and then...

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.430
Isn't that... Akira?!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:26.180
Wow, what a small face. Almost like a tangerine.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.720
All right! Here I go!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.310
W-W-Wait, please!

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.150
M-Me...

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.110
Please battle me!

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.280
What?!

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.530
She's...

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.280
...another Selector?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.820
Y-You two, too?

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.160
Who are these girls?

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:47.410
No way you're getting an autograph from Akira like that. How rude!

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:51.000
Ah? N-No... I'm...

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.290
Thanks for being my fan!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.170
You want my autograph, right?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.420
Let's go someplace else, then! You girls, too!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.340
Come on, Ruuko!

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.140
Akira's way too generous.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.520
<b>Permitted
Not
Access
Unauthorized</b>

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:10.540
Over here!
<b>Permitted
Not
Access
Unauthorized</b>

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.230
Over here!

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:22.450
There's <i>so</i> many Selectors here! Akira's in luck! Aki-lucky!

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.240
Um, I...

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.120
Let's get a battle done before class starts, okay?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.330
Now, who's first?

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.290
Um...

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.790
You're first, right? What's your name?

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.920
H-Hi-Hitoe...

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:38.840
Nice! A friendly battle between Hitoe and Akira is about to starty-starty!

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.300
Open!

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:21.630
When a battle field is opened, any Eternal Girl candidate in close vicinity is drawn into this world.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:22.510
Hanayo-san!

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:23.920
Wh-What is this?!

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.470
Tama!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.140
You're getting my hair all ruffled up, Tama!

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.470
It's starting!

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.770
I'll go first. Battle start!

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.860
Let's do this, Midoriko!

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.990
Leave it to me!

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.410
Aki-lucky's LRIG is Piruluk-tan!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.030
Let's go and stampy-stampy them out!

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.370
Understood.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.830
A green deck versus a blue deck?

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.420
That Hitoe girl might be easier to battle against.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.460
Draw! Enercharge, Midoriko-san! Grow!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.800
And finally, I summon Sparrow!

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.810
Sparrow, Attack!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.350
Yikes! Now <i>that</i> looks strong!

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.730
It worked...?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:26.070
If I manage Midoriko-san's
Grow smoothly, I just might...

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.240
Aww, I'm just so, <i>so</i> scared!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.870
Anyway, Piruluk-tan—
Maybe we should Grow, too.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.160
But I'm still really, really scared!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.120
I wonder what cards Hitoe has in her hand?

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.380
I'm scared, so...

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:45.130
I'll have Hitoe discard one.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:51.590
I'm going to choose one of your cards, okay?

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.060
Can you toss it away?

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.720
Spell! Too Bad!

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:01.850
Let me see... got it! I bet it's a level 3 card!

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:02.690
Expose.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.820
Bullseye! Aki-lucky!

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:08.900
The card vanished?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.950
It's a strategy available to blue decks.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:14.740
They can forcibly make their opponent discard.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.200
No...

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.620
Piruluk-tan, Grow! Let's freeze
Hitoe's Sparrow while we're at it.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.460
Turn it to ice right where it stands.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.840
Nice and frozen! Sleep tight until the next turn!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.630
Wh-What should I do?

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:36.220
I only have two cards in my hand... I can't...

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.470
Calm down, Hitoe!

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.520
Don't get too surprised yet!

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.100
I still have a <i>lot</i> more in store. Right, Piruluk?

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.070
Arts. Peeping Analyze.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:54.530
And now, I'll have you throw away <i>all</i>
the cards of the level I'm going to tell you.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:55.200
A-All?!
And now, I'll have you throw away <i>all</i>
the cards of the level I'm going to tell you.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.080
A-All?!

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.040
What should I pick? Level... 1? Or 2?

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.250
This looks bad! Her expression will give it away!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.250
3... 4...

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:14.140
There we go. Throw away your level 4 cards!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.980
It's a throw-away festival, isn't it?

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:33.650
You know what, let me guess why you want to be an Eternal Girl while we're at it.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.500
Poor girl...

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.000
She has no friends.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.090
We've got ourselves a loner here!
Can I get <i>your</i> autograph?!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.050
Hitoe, you can't! The battle is still going on!
We've got ourselves a loner here!
Can I get <i>your</i> autograph?!

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:54.090
Hitoe, you can't! The battle is still going on!

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.550
Don't listen to her!

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.010
How awful...

00:08:59.010 --> 00:08:59.810
Yuzuki-san?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.850
I'm gonna stop this battle!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:07.350
I know! I'll interfere, just like how
Kazuki did to stop our battle the other day!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.190
Don't do it.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:08.900
Why not?!

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.990
It wasn't Kazuki who stopped the battle. It was the teacher.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:20.120
Someone who knew nothing about the cards—an irregular—stepped in.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.740
And...

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:26.750
Stopping a battle on purpose is met with severe penalty.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:30.630
A penalty, you say?!
What Akira's doing is a lot worse!

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.710
She's not breaking any rules.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:33.340
But...!

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:37.260
This battle is cruel.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.140
<i>But...</i>

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.310
Tama?

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.860
Go, Piruluk-tan.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.240
Hitoe!

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.490
My... Life Cloth is all gone...

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.570
Don't give up yet! Guard against the attack!

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:05.040
What's the use? I'm going to lose anyway...

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.500
Believe in me, Hitoe!

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.380
Hitoe...

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:32.980
Midoriko!

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:42.780
Game over. It's Akira's win.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.010
Sorry...

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.900
I'm sorry... sorry...

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:18.740
I gave up the fight... but Midoriko is
the one in pain now... I'm really sorry...

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.740
U-Um...

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.030
Hitoe-san?

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.500
So, who's going to battle me next?

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.130
Hey, Piruluk-tan?

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:37.050
You're so fast to fall asleep...

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:41.760
Then we'll have our battle tomorrow!
Here, let's exchange email addresses!

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:44.760
I-I don't have a mobile phone...

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.770
No way! Super rare! How about you then?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.520
Well...

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:50.770
Yuzuki...

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.110
Sorry, but we have to run!

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:04.950
I won't let you go until you share your address.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.090
Ruuko!

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.960
Did you get an earful for being late?

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:26.300
Yeah, I was told to stand in the hall...
then again, I got to skip out on math class.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.510
Aki-lucky!

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.180
Stop that.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.140
There's no way I can beat a girl that good.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.060
Well, you still gave her your address.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:38.150
'Cause there was no other way we could've gotten away!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.360
I could battle Akira-san if you want...

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.900
Don't worry.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.860
As long as you don't agree
to battle, everything's fine.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:48.330
Yeah, that's right...

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:52.120
I was only watching from outside,
but Akira-san looked really strong.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:55.080
Hitoe, that other girl, was strong as well.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:58.840
I didn't know the Eternal Girl
candidates were on this high a level...

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.760
Am I... capable of taking them all on?

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.550
I know! Yuzuki, why don't you update your deck?

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.600
My deck? You mean, at the card shop?

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.140
Right. Is there a problem?

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.140
No...

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.150
I've never gone to one before. I want to go!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.440
Well, let's go together then.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.070
Okay!

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:30.280
I didn't know there was a card shop around here.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.750
You sure know a lot about cards, Kazuki-kun.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:38.960
Yeah. I've been playing WIXOSS for a long time now.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.760
I got Yuzuki to play it, too, and her deck happened to have Hanayo-san in it.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.130
Right, Yuzuki?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.510
Ah—yeah, right.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.260
Here we are.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.870
Available
50 Seats
Dueling Space
Trading Card Specialty Store

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:53.850
Here?

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:01.770
This place feels kinda... mature, in a way.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.910
Hey, Kazuki-kun!

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.120
We just got a new series of WIXOSS!

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:19.290
You're here too, Yuzuki-chan! It's been a while!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.290
H-Hello.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.750
We wanted to update Yuzuki's deck.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.340
Do you think you could help us?

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.970
Sure! I'd do anything to help Yuzuki-chan!

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.300
I mean, I love cute girls, you know.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:37.390
Yuzuki-chan's deck is Red Ambition, so...

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:42.110
it should cycle a lot better with an Adamasphere.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:45.780
Isn't Adamasphere one of the cards in the new series?

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:49.700
Right, but the singles aren't freely available yet.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.790
No luck so far...

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.460
What about these cards?

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:06.260
It's a bit of a waste, but they don't match well with Yuzuki's deck.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.380
Then, do you mind if I have just this one card?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:11.140
Huh?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:17.680
Just a hunch, but I think I can pay for this using my colorless SIGNIs.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.940
Wow, right on!

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:23.690
I'm surprised you knew that. That's some high-level stuff!

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.620
I guess we have to wait for the singles to come out.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.870
For now, you just have to get
better with the deck you have.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.080
Okay, it's your turn, Yuzuki.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:42.830
I'll draw this, and charge. Grow.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.170
Wait a minute. Can you show me your hand?

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:48.300
You've stopped at level 2 again.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.550
You can perform better with a
solid Grow strategy, you know?

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.180
B-But...

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:57.470
This won't do. Your battle style is way too straightforward, Yuzuki.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.640
What's wrong with being straightforward?!

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.440
Huh?

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.320
I'm... I'm going to bed!

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:09.110
Yuzuki?

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.390
<i>Yuzuki is Kazuki's bride!</i>

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.270
<i>How cute.</i>

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.440
<i>That's no good!</i>

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.810
<i>Sisters and brothers can't get married!</i>

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:52.320
<i>Everyone's going to say you're a bad girl! They really will!</i>

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.070
<i>Bad girl...</i>

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.330
<i>Yuzuki-chan!</i>

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.630
Straightforward battles...

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:14.470
Being straightforward... being honest...

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:18.010
Why is that a bad thing?

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:22.890
<b>Akira
Mail Received</b>

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.060
Akira...

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:29.820
"Who's going to fight me?
Yuzu-pon or Ruu-Ruu?"

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.660
I can't lose...!

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.790
You wait here, Tama.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.090
I feel sorry for Hitoe-san...

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.920
<i>But...</i>

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:06.140
I wonder why... for some reason, I want to battle Akira-san.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.730
B-But that's not good, right?

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.650
I mean, everyone is battling so earnestly for their wishes.

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.070
Battle!

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:30.330
Hey, Tama, could asking for Grandma to live a long and healthy life be a wish?

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:51.810
Huh? You're not with Kazuki-kun?

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.190
Yeah. He said he had to do something.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.530
I see...

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:58.400
You're not going to get that?

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:05.010
She's kind of creepy...

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.580
This email says she's coming here to get you.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.590
Hey, Ruuko, let's stop by somewhere before we go home!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.920
I guess that's okay...

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.470
Hey, let's go here!

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:27.350
Karaoke?

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:30.810
The boxes are private, so it'll be hard for Akira to find us here.

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:35.230
But it's my first time singing karaoke. What song should I pick?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.860
Just figure it out when we get in!

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:40.900
No, no, no, wait! These kinds of things need to be clear first!

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.490
I've got to strategize for the long term!

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:44.700
Strategize?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.580
Yes, because... huh?

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.120
Kazuki...

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:55.040
Isn't that the girl who works at the card shop?

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.630
Momoka-san... right?

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.220
It looks like that something
had to do with Momoka-san.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.300
Hey, maybe it's a date—

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.680
Shut up!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.560
Y-Yuzuki-san...

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.480
Ruuko, you're a bit... different.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.060
Like how you don't even have wishes and stuff...

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.320
When you saw that horrible battle...

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:27.160
You saw that Hitoe was hurt, but you were looking at it as if nothing had happened...

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.790
W-Wait, I didn't mean...

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.290
I don't know what you're thinking, Ruuko!

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:40.050
What I'm thinking...?

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:49.430
That's ri... probably right...

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:05.110
I-I demand satisfaction!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.620
Please b-battle me!

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.290
Huh?

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.340
Got you!

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.840
You were running all over the place,
so I had no idea what to do anymore!

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:29.800
It must be my Aki-lucky day to find you here!

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:31.720
Akira...

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:37.850
Now, let's battle! Let's have an Aki-rendezvous! Let's have fun together! And...

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:40.820
Let me tear you apart.

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:47.410
Sure...

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:51.490
I was just looking for a way to
blow off some steam.

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:55.020
That
Meeting
was
Toxic

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:28.420
I shouldn't win...

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:30.300
Piruluk-tan, look into her!

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:32.090
Tama? Did you just...

00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:34.600
Open!

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:36.430
The wind feels good.

00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:37.560
This peace is nonsensical.

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.980
This
Peace
is
Nonsensical
